{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116388","id":3291974843,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7EN4y7","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116388","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116388.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116388.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116388","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116388/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116388/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116388/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/4d69c363fcb507f0fd919f67a3e98c898e0c5617","number":116388,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Rework GraphEditArranger","user":{"login":"Ardot66","id":142978236,"node_id":"U_kgDOCIWsvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142978236?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ardot66","html_url":"https://github.com/Ardot66","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ardot66/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ardot66/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ardot66/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ardot66/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ardot66/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ardot66/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ardot66/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ardot66/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ardot66/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolves #87492\r\nResolves #60300\r\nMight fix issues  #77739 and #75936\r\n\r\nThis completely replaces the existing GraphEditArranger implementation with a much more maintainable and generally improved algorithm.\r\n\r\nThe new algorithm follows the following steps:\r\n1. Data is taken from the GraphEdit and formed into a useful tree-like datastructure for arranging.\r\n2. The graph is split into connected chunks, and an ideal start node is found in each one.\r\n3. From the start node, every node in each chunk chooses a particular node to be arranged by. Nodes attempt to place themselves the most connections away from the start node as possible, with the least number of 'turns' as possible (turns being a change in the direction of connection being traversed)\r\n4. Nodes are arranged based on the node they chose to be arranged by. To avoid overlaps, nodes are 'bumped' out of each-other's way.\r\n5. A final pass is taken that bumps nodes off of connections, which can seriously impact readability otherwise.\r\n\r\nBased on my testing, this is a significant improvement over the previous arranger in essentially every way. This is especially apparent for graphs that have interconnections across branches, which the old arranger struggles with immensely.\r\n\r\nThere are certainly improvements that can be made to my new algorithm (see image 6), but I think that it's in a good enough state to be merged at the moment.\r\n\r\nI've tried to make both the code and algorithm that I wrote as readable and ideally maintainable as possible, which should be a serious improvement over the old algorithm, which I was completely unable to read. (my original plan was to just improve the old algorithm, but that didn't work out)\r\n\r\n## Gallery\r\n\r\n### 1. New Arranger\r\n<img width=\"838\" height=\"434\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/81241070-5f91-405a-85bf-0ea6ee824d80\" />\r\n\r\n### 2. Old Arranger\r\n<img width=\"626\" height=\"393\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d96d5bc2-6785-4b5b-b648-8ac23247666b\" />\r\n\r\n### 3. New Arranger\r\n<img width=\"747\" height=\"466\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/265e98df-12e3-4ce5-aeb9-488d7306995f\" />\r\n\r\n### 4. Old Arranger\r\nAdmittedly, the old one is on par with my arranger for this particular case, and probably many others.\r\n<img width=\"646\" height=\"648\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/49c2e814-e995-4099-8699-236e21d3eeb4\" />\r\n\r\n### 5. Arranged by me\r\nThis is just for reference so you can see how the graph should ideally look.\r\n<img width=\"892\" height=\"706\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/24ae8a83-2bf0-4424-95d6-57806fdd3499\" />\r\n\r\n### 6. New Arranger\r\n<img width=\"1005\" height=\"672\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8f8787c3-e329-4063-bad7-9efd12f936ba\" />\r\n\r\n### 7. Old Arranger\r\n<img width=\"533\" height=\"871\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1f0205ce-289e-4fe9-ab94-66e79926c4ee\" />\r\n\r\n### 8. New Arranger\r\nThe original version of my new arranger struggled with this kind of graph, and there are still minor issues with larger variations, however I still think it is a significant improvement.\r\n<img width=\"250\" height=\"871\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/38ceb265-ed56-4ddc-83f7-01389aab37d7\" />\r\n\r\n### 9. Old Arranger\r\n<img width=\"202\" height=\"872\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b3baa657-3613-4bcb-922e-d35326f7de94\" />\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":419752642,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0MTk3NTI2NDI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:visualscript","name":"topic:visualscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_